8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97469" :question/problem "Given that $X∼B(7,0.7),$ compute $P(X=5).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(7,0.7),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{x})(0.7)^{x}(0.3)^{7-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =f(5) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{5})(0.7)^{5}(0.3)^{7-5} \\\\  & =21(0.7)^{5}(0.3)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.3177\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $4$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97469/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fde5f8-b1e8-5903-b875-94b4403cb282"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97469"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-96728"] :question/problem "Given that $X∼B(4,0.2),$ compute $P(X=3).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(4,0.2),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{x})(0.2)^{x}(0.8)^{4-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{3})(0.2)^{3}(0.8)^{4-3} \\\\  & =4(0.2)^{3}(0.8) \\\\  & ≈0.0256\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $4$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-97468/selection/d2017ea237c34e7f26fec157264f1bbe2de731a474dd265f577c3989d426e454" :answer/id #uuid "349523