 answer to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(6,0.8),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{x})(0.8)^{x}(0.2)^{6-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4) & =f(4) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{4})(0.8)^{4}(0.2)^{6-4} \\\\  & =15(0.8)^{4}(0.2)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.2458\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $4$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97468/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fde5f8-b1e8-5903-b875-94b4403cb282"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97468"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97464/selection/41359325f4a56c92f24afe617354558e8995f8b15b20355b66fd27d38e58c48e" :answer/id #uuid "1ad8c383-ac77-5c25-a721-7191117bd471" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2765" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97464/selection/03ab3b50cb9f3cb08f9672d96ea313951dc4b9f69f23fcecca13aa44d2db2ad7" :answer/id #uuid "b155974d-c34f-57f6-946c-44c551fe2249" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1792" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97464/selection/c08182fab700405063c8da088d0afad108049b973969033badc833c77639e728" :answer/id #uuid "aff190c3-45ef-5b3f-97df-98069e7f96e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2443" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97464/selection/e265f5a9801c7000ebdfdb66942e135d60ddbb3813bbbe39d6c486241aa21aee" :answer/id #uuid "6ecc152b-c735-57ff-9a71-8628dd46a509" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3557" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97464/selection/dcd4de8888815a7c51dde16553875e06282f0ddc6a9c55e8678ab5eae698b059" :answer/id #uuid "5b75be13-1422-54e1-b280-4dd346