is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(4,\\frac{1}{3}),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{x}){(\\frac{1}{3})}^{x}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3) & =P(X\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{0}){(\\frac{1}{3})}^{0}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{1}){(\\frac{1}{3})}^{1}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4-1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}){(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4-2} \\\\  & =1{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{0}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4}+4{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{1}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{3}+6{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129971/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a03ad88-dc53-582c-b2ed-1aeb0ee2d0f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129971"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279689/field-1/e148328cd517bdebaa042200a5a4a0d9eb6cd3cb62aac30eb85aca970a2ad65c" :answer/id #uuid "a4c373b2-6846-57fe-91e4-661b3e90f018" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.156" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279689/field-1/0b655060625fa7cdca393844b07e6309896190bd10320208461f3ede3ab3587e" :answer/id #uuid "d054f0df-7150-5ca4-ba38-3a0fca355244" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.157" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279689/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "db030ad3-a850-5509-b07d-29e82f7de5f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279689/field-1/e148328cd517bdebaa042200a5a4a0d9eb6cd3cb62aac30eb85aca970a2ad65c" :answer-field/choices ["q-279689/field-1/e148328cd517bdebaa042200a5a4a0d9eb6cd3cb62aac30eb85aca970a2ad65c" "q-279689/field-1/0b655060625fa7cdca393844b07e6309896190bd10320208461f3ede3ab3587e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279689" :question/id #uuid "c318c44f-85fb-5bf9-8eb6-be0c12f47d85" :question/math-academy-id "q-279689" :question/problem "If $X∼B(3,\\frac{3}{4}),$ then, **rounded to $3$ decimal places**, $P(X<2)≈${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial, we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(3,\\frac{3}{4}),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{x}){(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & =P(X\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{0}){(\\frac{3}{4})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}){(\\frac{3}{4})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3-1} \\\\  & =1{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3}+3{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.156\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279689/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a03ad88-dc53-582c-b2ed-1aeb0ee2d0f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279689"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97510/selection/f2278669f3cf62cde0a9da9201389b464960971917c620c531a69ad8db84fe68" :answer/id #uuid "84ab08db-6d25-5bb8-a6be-bd204ee0b9f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0170" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97510/selection/bdcf3aecacbcc565c091d00e468e57c3ccab7f14ddc1664e942b120435eb2d7a" :answer/id #uuid "1c95acd7-d2ca-5c0c-85db-239033158d7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0016" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97510/selection/1a5acc2d47bcf23f5d25e06ec12688d1ac0856a10da1d8cab37e476b7897b099" :answer/id #uuid "9bbdaf