  & =f(5)+f(6) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{5})(0.2)^{5}(0.8)^{6-5}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{6})(0.2)^{6}(0.8)^{6-6} \\\\  & =6(0.2)^{5}(0.8)+1(0.2)^{6}(0.8)^{0} \\\\  & =0.0016.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97510/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a03ad88-dc53-582c-b2ed-1aeb0ee2d0f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97510"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279694/field-1/707dacca486637cf1e648f6a1ec95bc250f313d93ae2ea09a90a866b4fb47def" :answer/id #uuid "c9ce2808-63c0-52d2-91ac-e5e4c5f64329" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.210" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279694/field-1/2c7beb7e35afb423d74f2e4a410e0cd1018398222bb253109f4170126ea98c6f" :answer/id #uuid "c137a638-b505-528b-b6b9-9497934aa14b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.211" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279694/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbee166d-2db6-5b2f-ae47-3dcc4d488d44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279694/field-1/707dacca486637cf1e648f6a1ec95bc250f313d93ae2ea09a90a866b4fb47def" :answer-field/choices ["q-279694/field-1/707dacca486637cf1e648f6a1ec95bc250f313d93ae2ea09a90a866b4fb47def" "q-279694/field-1/2c7beb7e35afb423d74f2e4a410e0cd1018398222bb253109f4170126ea98c6f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279694" :question/id #uuid "d98302b0-e333-52fa-a5fb-5d15d4a044ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-279694" :question/problem "If $X∼B(5,\\frac{2}{3}),$then, **rounded to $3$ decimal places**, $P(X<3)≈${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial, we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(5,\\frac{2}{3}),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{5-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3) & =P(X\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{5-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{5-1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2}){(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{5-2} \\\\  & =1{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{0}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{5}+5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{1}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4}+10{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{3} \\\\  & ≈0.210\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279694/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a03ad88-dc53-582c-b2ed-1aeb0ee2d0f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279694"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97503/selection/c44fe4f0a16aba930aab5343f5d4cc6d58cda9e77787ba9aa489d0bd052ce31c" :answer/id #uuid "71ebf976-0cad-5e85-b510-fb3f662d1332" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.216" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97503/selection/3d442cffd13050216e5bbf16cf8738897a00ae015613cf785b8d81e95824820b" :answer/id #uuid "af842a20-ebb2-5fdd-8720-1f126adee9f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.227" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97503/selection/f31b1c8781cc2c908c29123f7e7b5e2a513e256aa7b331c6b0234462a11794b7" :answer/id #uuid "bb84c7e5-f5e4-5cab-98d4-101aad6aa369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.154" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97503/selection/e5a60b4745cd7963ae17cdf0aa3803f2a21ca4093240cc9429da5b68cb249cd7" :answer/id #uuid "b91fa5a2-ef29-5a68-b9a5-9e1deb4463e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.273" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97503/selection/89ea20d0211adec86f2cf7addcc2251cde829a7f1f7bab8924e6f7898bb20876" :answer/id #uuid "d1b72df0-f121-5c1f-b6ae-e1185972a0f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.189" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97503/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aaa042bb-7e24-580b-a788-279d54808311" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97503/selection/c44fe4f0a16aba930aab5343f5d4cc6d58cda9e77787ba9aa489d0bd052ce31c" :answer-field/choices ["q-97503/selection/c44fe4f0a16aba930aab5343f5d4cc6d58cda9e77787ba9aa489d0bd052ce31c" "q-97503/selection/3d442cffd13050216e5bbf16cf8738897a00ae015613cf785b8d81e95824820b" "q-97503/selection/f31b1c8781cc2c908c29123f7e7b5e2a513e256aa7b331c6b0234462a11794b7" "q-97503/selection/e5a60b4745cd7963ae17cdf0aa3803f2a21ca4093240cc9429da5b68cb249cd7" "q-97503/selection/89ea20d0211adec86f2cf7addcc2251cde829a7f1f7bab8924e6f7898bb20876"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97503" :question/id #uuid "f656f5f8-5266-5801-8598-ae2960a27fa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-97503" :question/problem "Given that $X∼B(3,0.3),$ compute $P(X\\ge 2).$" :question/worked-solution "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ where $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success on each trial,  we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(3,0.3),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{x})(0.3)^{x}(0.7)^{3-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(X\\in {2,3}) \\\\  & =f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2})(0.3)^{2}(0.7)^{3-2}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3})(0.3)^{3}(0.7)^{3-3} \\\\  & =3(0.3)^{2}(0.7)+1(0.3)^{3}(0.7)^{0} \\\\  & =0.216.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97503/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a03ad88-dc53-582c-b2ed-1aeb0ee2d0f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97503"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12997